# ProWeb Sheet Python

A Python-based spreadsheet application inspired by the attached browser spreadsheet, rebuilt with a Flask backend and a lightweight browser UI.

## Features

- Editable grid in the browser
- Formula evaluation for basic spreadsheet functions
- CSV import/export
- XLSX export
- Simple cell selection and formula bar

## Run

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
```

Then open: http://localhost:5000

## Structure

- `app.py` — Flask app and routes
- `spreadsheet_core.py` — spreadsheet engine and formula evaluator
- `templates/index.html` — UI shell
- `static/app.js` — frontend logic
- `static/styles.css` — styling

## Notes

This is a Python conversion of the browser prototype and focuses on a working spreadsheet engine with core functionality rather than a complete reimplementation of every advanced feature from the JavaScript version.

## Next possible upgrades

- Undo/redo stack
- Cell styles and formatting
- Freeze panes and row/column resizing
- Multi-sheet support
- Advanced formulas and imported workbook compatibility
